/* Guide */
"guia.titulo" = "Guide";
"guia.intro" = "This guide explains the method step by step. The app does for you the “Terminal” steps that appear in it.";

/* Why? */
"porque.titulo" = "Why does this happen?";
"porque.1" = "Your iPhone is a two-storey house. Upstairs is the system (iOS). Downstairs, your things: photos, messages, apps.";
"porque.2" = "Before updating, a “guard” checks whether the new system fits. Since you were really tight on space, it says: “it fits”.";
"porque.3" = "The iPhone removes the old system. But when reserving room for the new one, the storage has a rule the guard doesn't know about: you can't reserve more than ~84% of the free space all at once. It doesn't fit… and upstairs is left empty. Downstairs nothing has been touched.";
"porque.4" = "The fix tells the guard that the system is a little bigger than it really is. Then the guard says “it doesn't fit” and the iPhone tidies up its temporary files (caches, logs…). With that gap, the real system does fit.";
"porque.riesgo" = "**Risk:** the clean-up may delete caches and things that download again. In the real case nothing was missing. If it fails, the iPhone stays as it was (in recovery mode, with your data) and you can try again.";
"porque.video" = "Coming soon: a video that explains it right here.";

